            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LovesCheese"
            },
            "reviewBody": "All of those reviews are just silly. If you want a potato salad with celery and onions and paprika and other things, I'm sure you can find such a recipe on this website. Why mess with one whose entire appeal is its simplicity? Treating it as a \"base\" recipe is one thing, going on about all the extra things it \"needs\" is another. Great dish for the younger guests at summer BBQs, since lots of kids are picky about onions and things."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Using a creamy salad dressing is brilliant. It's already seasoned. Now you can make \"ranch potato salad\" or \"blue cheese potato salad.\" And if you want to add celery, onion or anything else go ahead.",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-02T19:07:51.583Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MatureLeek2277"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the perfect recipe. You can change it up if you prefer by using Duke's Mayonnaise and relish or a little dill spice and sweet vinegar instead of the dressing. The basic recipe I use is potatoes, eggs, sweet relish, and Duke's mayonnaise which is a always a hit. My friend doesn't like crunchy things in her food so I just use the relish juice. Sometimes I add mustard and/or onions for more flavor but it is not really needed.",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-02T15:18:12.072Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chris2011"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I needed to use up some red potatoes and miracle whip. I used about 3x the potatoes and 5 eggs and made like the recipe stated. I ran out of miracle whip so added a bit of mayo as well as salt pepper and a tbsp of prepared mustard. Looks great and tasted great even warm.",
            "datePublished": "2018-02-09T09:48:17.157Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are nice instructions for a beginner making potato salad. I cubed my potatoes before boiling, and they were done in 10 minutes. I preferred it with a big squirt of yellow mustard stirred in.",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-18T02:28:22.583Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ChillyRice1371"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I always boil the eggs and potatoes - already diced or sliced - in the same pan starting with cold water - keep an eye on the potatoes and when they are just done the eggs will be too",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-02T22:38:30.332Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GRAMMA GORGEOUS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is like my mother used to make and what our family still makes using Miracle Whip Salad Dressing, except we add salt and pepper to taste, finely minced onion also to taste, about a teaspoon of yellow mustard, and mix the whole diced egg in too.\r\nBe sure to use red potatoes boiled in their skins til fork tender, then cool in cold water, peel and dice. Mixed while still warm the flavors of the dressing will really meld with the potato and hard cooked diced egg.\r\nChill for several hours or overnight for the best flavor!",
            "datePublished": "2005-03-24T12:46:28.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "blueartemis4"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made some small changes to the recipe, and I was very happy with the end result! I used Kraft Light Mayo, red potatoes, and two hard-boiled eggs. I stirred in unmeasured quantities of salt, pepper, and garlic powder (I used quite a bit of pepper and garlic powder, but not as much salt). I then sprinkled more pepper and paprika on the top when I added the crumbled egg yolks. It was very tasty!",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-05T16:31:59.960Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "janmauss"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Although the percentage of potato and egg is about right, this salad has way too much dressing for me. Plus cooking whole potatoes takes way too long--dice them before hand and they will be done in 10 minutes. It's just is too plain for our tastes. I'm not going to go on about how it could be improved to suit my families tastes, but this seems like a waste of ingredients",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-02T17:22:23.468Z"
          },
